module

public import Rule30Open.Foundations.Evolve
public import Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30EtherThree

/-!
# Under the center column `00001`, column 1 at the first white step has no `11` and no `1001`

Let the center column repeat the block `00001` and look at the right half it drives (the kit's `Rule30Ether.drv`),
from any initial right half, finite or not. At the first white step of each period, the step just after the black
one, column 1 never reads `11` or `1001` with the last reading at time 29 or later: its 1s are isolated and none of
its runs of 0s has length exactly 2.

* `rankTabs`, `rk`, `nodeOK`, `partOK`: a rank certificate over the states (phase, window of columns 1..12, last
  three readings at the first white steps). Rank 0 states go to rank 0 states for both values of column 13 and
  complete no forbidden word; a state of positive rank goes to states of smaller rank. Ranks are at most 29. `ok_p`,
  `parts_ok`: the kernel checks, one per phase.
* `Runs00001.rank_bound`: along the driven right half, the rank at time `t` is at most `29 - t`.
* `no_11_time_00001`, `no_1001_time_00001`: the forbidden words, stated for the times of the readings.
* `runs_00001`: the same for the readings `reading R ph i` of column 1 at the `i`-th first white step, `i ≥ 5`.
* `Runs00001.evolve_eq_drv`, `runs_00001_evolve`: for every row whose center column repeats `00001` from time `T`,
  the readings of column 1 at the times `T + 5 i`, `i ≥ 5`, avoid the two words.

The natural-language argument is `Runs00001.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata Rule30Ether Rule30EtherThree Rule30StripCertificates

/-! The certificate and the helpers live in `Runs00001`; the headline theorems are in `Rule30Open`. -/

namespace Runs00001

